# Platform fee at checkout (buyer UI)

**Platform fee** (town flat / convenience fee) and **COD surcharges** are KoyaKart pass-through charges. Buyers must see them **only at checkout or payment**, with a **line-by-line breakdown** — never baked into browse/catalog totals.

## Browse phase (catalog, sticky dock, floating bar)

Show **goods / service subtotal only** (tests, packages, glam services, laundry pieces, grocery `payableSubtotal`).

- Do **not** add platform fee or COD fee to dock/bar headline amounts.
- Subtitle hint is OK: e.g. “fees at checkout”, “Platform fee shown before you pay”.
- **Service-specific charges** tied to the product (e.g. diagnostics **home collection**, glam **home visit**, laundry **pickup/drop**) may appear in browse subtotals when the product cannot be booked without them — but **platform fee never** in browse totals.

## Checkout phase (bill summary, confirm sheet, pay button, gateway)

Show full payable total with explicit rows:

- Goods / services subtotal  
- Home collection / travel / delivery (if applicable)  
- **Platform fee** (label clearly — “Platform fee” or “Service fee”)  
- COD handling (if COD selected)  
- **Amount payable** / Pay now total  

Grocery **Basket** page sticky footer is checkout — including platform fee there is correct.

## Vertical reference

| Vertical    | Browse total              | Checkout breakdown        |
|------------|---------------------------|---------------------------|
| Grocery    | Sticky cart = items only  | Cart bill + sticky pay    |
| Diagnostics| Dock = tests/packages     | Step 2 bill + book button |
| Laundry    | Dock = pieces + travel    | Confirm sheet + platform  |
| Glam       | Dock subtotal w/o platform| Confirm sheet + platform  |

When adding a new vertical, follow the same split unless product explicitly documents otherwise.
